{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Monte Carlo Methods \u2014 Learning from Complete Episodes Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: rollout \u2192 list of (s, a, r)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rollout(env, policy, max_steps=200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trajectory = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = env.reset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_steps):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a = policy(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        trajectory.append((s, a, r))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = s_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return trajectory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "No model, only `env.reset()` and `env.step(s, a)`. Same interface as a gym environment but stripped down."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: compute returns (reverse sweep)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def returns_from(trajectory, gamma):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    G = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _, _, r in reversed(trajectory):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        G = r + gamma * G"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        returns.append(G)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return list(reversed(returns))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "One pass, `O(T)`. The backward recurrence `G_t = r_{t+1} + \u03b3 G_{t+1}` avoids re-summing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: first-visit MC evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mc_policy_evaluation(env, policy, episodes, gamma=0.99):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    V = defaultdict(float)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    counts = defaultdict(int)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(episodes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        trajectory = rollout(env, policy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        returns = returns_from(trajectory, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        seen = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for t, ((s, _, _), G) in enumerate(zip(trajectory, returns)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if s in seen:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            seen.add(s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            counts[s] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            V[s] += (G - V[s]) / counts[s]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return V"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three lines do the work: mark state as seen on first visit, increment count, update running mean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: \u03b5-greedy MC control (on-policy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def mc_control(env, episodes, gamma=0.99, epsilon=0.1):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Q = defaultdict(lambda: {a: 0.0 for a in ACTIONS})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    counts = defaultdict(lambda: {a: 0 for a in ACTIONS})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def policy(s):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if random() < epsilon:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return choice(ACTIONS)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return max(Q[s], key=Q[s].get)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(episodes):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        trajectory = rollout(env, policy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        returns = returns_from(trajectory, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        seen = set()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for (s, a, _), G in zip(trajectory, returns):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if (s, a) in seen:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            seen.add((s, a))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            counts[s][a] += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            Q[s][a] += (G - Q[s][a]) / counts[s][a]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return Q, policy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: compare to DP gold standard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Your MC estimate of `V^\u03c0` should agree with the DP result from Lesson 02 as episodes \u2192 \u221e. In practice: 50,000 episodes on 4\u00d74 GridWorld gets you within `~0.1` of the DP answer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement first-visit MC evaluation of the uniform-random policy on 4\u00d74 GridWorld. Run 10,000 episodes. Plot `V(0,0)` as a function of episode count against the DP answer.\n2. **Medium.** Implement \u03b5-greedy MC control with `\u03b5 \u2208 {0.01, 0.1, 0.3}`. Compare mean return after 20,000 episodes. What does the curve look like? Where does the bias-variance tradeoff live?\n3. **Hard.** Implement *off-policy* MC with importance sampling: collect data under uniform-random policy `\u03bc`, estimate `V^\u03c0` for the deterministic optimal policy `\u03c0`. Compare plain IS vs per-decision IS vs weighted IS. Which has lowest variance?"
      ]
    }
